────────────────────────────────────────
✅ Summary

| Property    | Ensures                                      |
| ----------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Atomicity   | All or nothing                               |
| Consistency | Rules/constraints kept; valid states         |
| Isolation   | Safe concurrency (by isolation level)        |
| Durability  | Committed data survives crashes              |

Interview one-liner:
“ACID means transactions are all-or-nothing, keep data valid, don’t improperly interfere when concurrent, and once committed stay durable after failures.”
